From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: odroid-go-ultra: GPU up to 666 MHz

In DOOM 3 BFG's soak test (doom3-test.py soak) with a memory checker
running beside it on the A73 cores, this board reads bit 42 of a 64-bit
word wrong in bursts on several cores at once: the line in the CPU cache
holds the wrong value, the DRAM the right one (memcheck reads it again
after "dc civac"). It happens in the first minutes of the soak, while the
Mali-G52 still runs at 800 MHz; later the ddr-thermal trip at 85 C holds
the GPU lower and the errors stop. GPU faults (DATA_INVALID, bad page
map), half a frozen screen and crashes in the game come with them.

Soaks with the GPU's top at 800 MHz: 4 out of 4 with errors (8, 3, 6 and
5 words); with the top at 666 MHz: 0 out of 5, from hot and cool
starts (342136 checker passes in the last). Frame rates stay as they
were: the game's dynamic resolution makes up for it. Turn off the
800 MHz operating point, 17 % of the GPU's clock.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
@@ -709,6 +709,17 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&gpu_opp_table {
+	/*
+	 * Under DOOM 3 at 800 MHz this board reads bit 42 of a 64-bit word
+	 * wrong now and then (the cache line wrong, the DRAM right): the GPU
+	 * stops at 666 MHz.
+	 */
+	opp-799999987 {
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
+
 &mipi_analog_dphy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
